      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Blackfeather Roost [zone=436]\n**Who:**\n- Ashrana [npc=23276]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 1\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n**Time Limit:** | 08:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Royal Crest [item=52167]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Captain Slarus [npc=23286]\n- Royal Guard [npc=23285]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Blackfeather Roost #1 - Blackfeather Roost, The Ledge [quest=3606]\n- Blackfeather Roost #2 - Blackfeather Roost, The Grove [quest=3632]\n- Blackfeather Roost #3 - Blackfeather Roost, The Cliffs [quest=3672]\n- Kill the Queen of the Harpies! [quest=3694]\n**Era:** | !Serpents Spine\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Sat Oct 7 03:48:45 2006\nModified: Sat Apr 20 08:23:17 2024 | | _There are six islands in Blackfeather Roost, each with its own requirements for access (you can port from island to island after completing a short task for each):_\n\\- The Base (entered from Goru'kar Mesa)\n\\- The First Ledge ( see this task [quest=3606])\n\\- The Harpy Grove ( see this task [quest=3632])\n\\- The Harpy Cliffs ( see this task [quest=3672])\n\\- The Harpy Mesa ( see this task [quest=3696])\n\\- The Royal Throne (complete this task)\n\n---\n\nAshrana is in Blackfeather Roost on the last isle before entering the Queen chambers.\nYou say, 'Hail, Ashrana'\nAshrana says 'My sister, Mestle, told me you had agreed to accept our challenge. I'm sure she bored you with threats and doom, but please allow me to tempt you instead. Great riches and treasure can be had at the end of this road if you walk it with me. Are you [interested]?'\nYou say, 'I am interested'\nAshrana says 'Excellent \\_\\_\\_. The situation is very simple as you'll soon see I'm sure. The fact is that I should be Queen, not my sad and weak sister Eletyl. I aim to [replace] her and assume my rightful role as leader of this Roost. Will you [help] me?'\nYou say, 'Replace her?'\nAshrana says 'It is far past time for the old to give way to the new and high time I take my rightful place in this roost. Will you [help] me accomplish this and reap the rewards?'\nYou say, 'I will help you'\nAshrana says 'Your role in this little Drama is quite simple - [Kill] my sister Eletyl, ransack her home and return to me. I will then assume my rightful role and place.'\nYou say, 'I will kill her'\nAshrana says 'There is one snag to our fine plan - getting to my dear older sister the Queen. You have learned to tame the Griffons of this Roost and move from place to place but a morsel of food will not be enough to accomplish this task. The Queen's abode can only be reached via specially trained Griffons. To ride these Griffons you need the [Royal Crest].'\nYou say, 'Royal crest?'\nAshrana says 'Captain Slarus leads the Queen's personal guard. Her loyalty to the Queen is unquestioned and so, of course, Slarus must die. But more than that Slarus and her top lieutenants alone have the magical Crest needed to command the Royal Griffons. Kill Slarus and retrieve a Crest for you and your companions. Return to me when you have done so.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Blackfeather Roost - Reach the royal throne'.\nCaptain Slarus leads the Queen's personal guard. Her loyalty to the Queen is unquestioned and so, of course, Slarus must die. But more than Slarus and her top lieutenants alone have the magical Crest needed to command the Royal Griffons. Kill Slarus and retrieve a Crest for you and your companions. Return to me when you have done so.\nKill the Captain of the Guard, Captain Slarus 0/1 (Blackfeather Roost)\n_Captain Slarus can hit for up to 1,700. He has four guards next to him while a fifth guard patrols the area. The trash mobs and guards have a quick respawn time, so you may need to deal with anywhere from 3 to 8 mobs at once to get this kill._\nKill the Royal Guards 0/5 (Blackfeather Roost)\n_The guards are clustered around Captain Slarus, close to the nest leading to the Queen's Palace. Neither guards nor the Captain see invis. All drop a Royal Crest. Captain Slarus will drop an item of loot of her own._\nReturn One Royal Crest to Ashrana 0/1 (Blackfeather Roost)\nAshrana says 'Aha! Well done \\_\\_\\_! Now we can finally [accomplish] our goal!'\nThis leads you in to the task 'Kill the Queen of the Harpies!'.\n_You are now able to use the griffon nest on the Mesa to reach the Queen's palace which leads to the last task in this series Kill the Queen of the Harpies! [quest=3694]._\n**Submitted by:** Lias Roxx, Defiant, Zek",
